<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine trade deficit widens to $1.8 bln Jan-May.</title>
<headline>Ukraine trade deficit widens to $1.8 bln Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukraine's trade deficit widened to $1.8 billion in the first five months from $1.6 billion in the same period last year and $0.33 billion between January and April, the Statistics Ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>			  UKRAINE MERCHANDISE TRADE</p>
<p>			  Jan-May 97     Jan-May 96     Jan-Apr 97</p>
<p> Exports (bln $)    5.137	    4.001	    4.734</p>
<p> Imports (bln $)    6.963	    5.571	    5.067</p>
<p> Balance (bln $)   -1.826	   -1.570	   -0.333</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are for trade with all countries. Trade with former Soviet republics resulted in a balance of minus $2.38 billion.</p>
<p>--Kiev Newsroom +38 044 244 9154</p>
